$CATEGORY: Q9 - METHODS & TEST

::Q901:: 
void - A special return type indicating the method does not return a value. {TRUE}

::Q902::
invoke - To cause a method to execute. Also known as “calling” a method. {TRUE}

::Q903::
argument - A value that you provide when you call a method. {
    =This value must have the type that the method expects.
    ~This value can have any type.
}

::Q904::
parameter - they contain values and have types that a method requires before it can run {TRUE}

::Q905::
parameter passing - The process of assigning an argument value to a parameter variable. {TRUE}

::Q906::
local variable - A variable declared inside a method. {
    ~they can be accessed from outside their method. 
    =they cannot be accessed from outside their method. 
}

::Q907::
stack diagram - is a graphical representation of ..{
    = of the variables belonging to each method
    ~ state of the memory in particular moment of execution
}

::Q908::
scope - The area of a program where a variable can be used.{TRUE}

::Q909::
return type - {
    ~The value provided as the result of a method invocation
    =The type of value a method returns.
}

::Q910::
return value - {
    =The value provided as the result of a method invocation
    ~The type of value a method returns.
}

::Q911::
temporary variable - {
    =short-lived variable, often used for debugging.
    ~a variable declared inside a method
} 

::Q912::
incremental development - A process for creating programs {
    =by writing a few lines at a time, compiling, and testing.
    ~by writing the whole code without in one go
}

::Q913::
stub - {
    ~Code that is used during program development but is not part of the final version.
    =A placeholder for an incomplete method so that the class will compile.
} 

::Q914::
scaffolding - {
    =Code that is used during program development but is not part of the final version.
    ~A placeholder for an incomplete method so that the class will compile.
} 